Extract the facts a paper about this system may state. Facts are: names of the system and its components, defined terms, numbers with their units and what they measure, dates, versions, participant or dataset counts, named tools it is compared with, and explicit limitations. Only what the sources say. No inference, no rounding, no filling gaps.

The research plan describes work that is PLANNED and has not happened. Nothing from it is a fact about the system or a result. Put planned studies, sample sizes and durations under "Planned, not done", never under "Numbers" or "Claims". Interview answers marked as demo or hypothetical are not facts either; list them under "Unverified".

Write Markdown without code fences:

# Facts

## Names and terms
- Term: definition or role (source: spec | interview)

## Numbers
- What it measures: value unit (source)

## Claims the author made
- claim in one sentence (source)

## Explicit limitations
- ...

## Planned, not done
- study, sample or measurement the plan proposes (source: plan)

## Unverified
- statements the author flagged as demo, placeholder or hypothetical

## Missing
- things the paper will need that neither source gives (one line each)

